# getServerSideProps (SSR)

This function runs **on every request** to the page. Use it when:

* The page needs data that changes frequently.
* The content depends on the user (authentication, cookies).
* You need access to request context (`req`, `res`).

```js
export async function getServerSideProps(context) {
  const data = await fetch('https://...');
  return { props: { data } };
}
```

**Downside:** Slower Time to First Byte (TTFB) because the server must fetch data on every hit.

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/dashboard.js
export default function Dashboard({ user }) {
  return <h1>Welcome, {user.name}</h1>;
}

export async function getServerSideProps(context) {
  // Read cookies from the request
  const { req } = context;
  const token = req.cookies.token;

  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/me', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
  });
  const user = await res.json();

  return { props: { user } };
}

// pages/old-page.js
export async function getServerSideProps() {
  return {
    redirect: {
      destination: '/new-page',
      permanent: true, // 301 redirect
    },
  };
}
